---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Über" description="About Me & De.">
  <article>
    <header class="post-head">
      <h1>Über</h1>
      <p class="post-meta">
        <span class="sq" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>about, roughly</span>
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I am learning German. This is where I file the evidence.
      </p>
      <p>
        Each post records something the German language does that an English
        speaker was not warned about. Posts are filed by
        <a href="https://www.coe.int/en/web/common-european-framework-reference-languages">CEFR</a>
        level, from A1 (<em>Breakthrough</em>) to C1 (<em>Effective Operational
        Proficiency</em> — the framework's own name for it, and I would not dream
        of improving it). As my German improves, the posts contain more German
        and fewer explanations. The plan is that by C1 this blog will be
        unreadable to the person who started it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Posts are short. There are no reading-time estimates, because the honest
        answer would be “longer than the word count suggests, if you stop to
        look things up, which is the point.”
      </p>
      <p>
        The name: <em>me and DE</em>, but also <em>mäandern</em> — to meander.
        Which is the method.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="tombstone" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <nav class="post-foot">
      <a href="/">← Inhalt</a>
    </nav>
  </article>
</Base>
